<title>FRANCE: Dassault suspended limit-down again.</title>
<headline>Dassault suspended limit-down again.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Dassault Aviation were suspended limit-down and a requote will be attempted at 0940 GMT, a spokeswoman for the French stockmarkets association SBF said on Monday.</p>
<p>Its opening had been delayed by an imbalance in orders.</p>
<p>The SBF spokeswoman said the new thresholds are 981 francs and 1,031 francs.</p>
<p>Dassault Aviation, which risks being nationalised if the privatisation of its merger partner Aerospatiale is scuppered, is down on the parliamentary election results.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
